column2:
You are made the Shri-elephant by the king; you are the leader of his elephants; the king will worship you with garlands and first food;
agnipuran:289:17	then the people at his order will worship you. You must guard the king in battle, on the road and at home.
agnipuran:289:18	Leaving the animal nature, remember the divine nature. In the war of gods and demons of old the Shri-elephant was made by the gods:
agnipuran:289:19	the glorious elephant named Arishta, son of Airavana. All the splendor of the Shri-elephants stands by him;
agnipuran:289:20	that splendor, lord of elephants, joined with divine nature, stand by you; blessings to you; protect the king in battle.
